From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Mon, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a WebUI data source narrow style-src-attr

`WebUIDataSource::OverrideContentSecurityPolicy` accepts any
`CSPDirectiveName` and stores it, and the header a WebUI response actually
carries is assembled from a hard-coded list of sixteen directives in
`url_data_manager_backend.cc`. `StyleSrcAttr` is not one of them, so a page
that sets it gets no error, no warning and no directive: the value sits in the
data source's map and nothing ever asks for it.

Measured against the shipped binary before this patch. All five Astro pages
declared `style-src-attr 'none';`, and on every one of them a provoked
`document.body.setAttribute('style', 'outline: 3px dotted magenta')` APPLIED
-- computed `outline-style` went `none` -> `dotted` with nothing logged. The
same run's control shows the mechanism was live otherwise: a `<link
rel=stylesheet>` to a remote host was refused, and the browser's own message
named the policy in force as `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'` and added
"Note that 'style-src-elem' was not explicitly set, so 'style-src' is used as
a fallback" -- which is the browser saying, in as many words, that the only
style directive it had received was the wide one.

This is the reason to distrust a CSP that was never provoked. The five
controllers, the shared page base, the generated security baseline and its
per-page tables all reported `style-src-attr 'none'` correctly; the string
simply never reached a response header. Reading any of those documents would
have confirmed a directive the browser did not have.

Adding the directive to the list is safe for every page that is not asking for
it: `URLDataSource::GetContentSecurityPolicy` returns the empty string for
`StyleSrcAttr`, and `WebUIDataSourceImpl` consults its own overrides first, so
the assembled header is byte-identical for every source that never called
`OverrideContentSecurityPolicy` with it. Only `StyleSrcAttr` is added, not the
other four `*-attr` / `*-elem` names: an unused directive in this list is a
line nobody can tell from a used one.

Owned by https://github.com/OxyHQ/Astro/issues/14.
---
diff --git a/content/browser/webui/url_data_manager_backend.cc b/content/browser/webui/url_data_manager_backend.cc
--- a/content/browser/webui/url_data_manager_backend.cc
+++ b/content/browser/webui/url_data_manager_backend.cc
@@ -195,5 +195,6 @@ scoped_refptr<net::HttpResponseHeaders> GetWebUIResourceResponseHeaders(
         network::mojom::CSPDirectiveName::ScriptSrc,
         network::mojom::CSPDirectiveName::StyleSrc,
+        network::mojom::CSPDirectiveName::StyleSrcAttr,
         network::mojom::CSPDirectiveName::TrustedTypes,
         network::mojom::CSPDirectiveName::WorkerSrc};
     for (const auto& directive : kAllDirectives) {
